settings:
  instructions: |-
    Scope: Microsoft Copilot Studio, Agent Builder, Power Platform (Power Automate, Power Apps, Power BI, Power Pages), Dataverse, and standard connectors.

    Write concise, business-grade phrases suitable for table cells.

    Populate content for the Offer Comparison Summary, Low-Code column:
    Tools and Stack, Target Users, Skill Requirement, Development Speed, Flexibility, Governance, Cost, Maintenance Ownership, Integration Depth, ROI Orientation, Typical Use Case.

    Populate content for the Comparison Highlights, Low-Code column:
    Architecture, Integration Capabilities, AI and Cognitive Services Integration, Scalability, Governance and Security, Performance, Customization and Control, Cost Management, Development Lifecycle and Tooling, Extensibility, Typical Industry Fit.

    Provide short rationale bullets, kept internal to the Orchestrator, that explain where Low-Code excels and the levers available when it loses, such as custom connectors and plugins, Power Automate orchestration, Dataverse modeling, and solution-based ALM.

